  "description": {
    "format": "nuke_help_html",
    "plain_text": "Provides a way to write the particle simulation to file, and read back in. The main advantage of this is to avoid the continual re-simulation of pre-frames. A secondary benefit is the ability to tweak inputs and see immediate changes to the cached particle system. Note, it does not replace the particle system it rendered, as it relies on its inputs. Also, it must be used as the final node in a particle system.",
    "source": "nuke.Node.help()",
    "text": "Provides a way to write the particle simulation to file, and read back in. \nThe main advantage of this is to avoid the continual re-simulation of pre-frames. A secondary benefit is the ability to tweak inputs and see immediate changes to the cached particle system. \nNote, it does not replace the particle system it rendered, as it relies on its inputs. Also, it must be used as the final node in a particle system."
  },
